# Regenerated per run, or machine-specific — never shared.
#
# The suites rebuild all three: .state holds Playwright storage states (which
# carry live Keycloak access tokens) plus the capability probe, .artifacts holds
# reports, screenshots, videos and traces, and node_modules comes from
# `pnpm install`.
*/node_modules/
*/.state/
*/.artifacts/
*/out/
scheduled_tasks.lock

# OpenReplay's vendored stack generates its own secrets on first run — JWT
# signing keys, S3 credentials, Postgres passwords. Recreate them locally with
# scripts/fetch-upstream.sh + scripts/up.sh rather than committing them.
skills/openreplay-stack/vendor/*.env
skills/openreplay-stack/vendor/docker-envs/

# Personal, not project policy. Attribution preferences and permission grants
# differ per person, and a shared settings.json applies one developer's choices
# to everyone's clone. See "Commit attribution" in CLAUDE.md for the settings
# this project's authors use. Remove this line if a genuinely team-wide setting
# ever needs committing.
settings.json
settings.local.json
